Laplacian edge detection
For Laplacian edge detection, we use the cv2.Laplacian() function of the OpenCV library. The algorithm of Laplacian edge detection is also based on the fact that at the edges, there is a drastic change in the pixel intensity. However, unlike Sobel edge detection, it uses the second derivative to find edges. It uses the fact that the second derivative is zero in the regions where there is a drastic change in pixel intensity.

This function requires two parameters, which are listed below:

The first parameter is the input image.
The second parameter is the data depth. For this, we use cv2.CV_64F. It means the NumPy array, dtype, is float64 (64-bit floating-point).
lap_Edge = cv2.Laplacian(gray, cv2.CV_64F)
cv2.imshow('Laplacian', lap_Edge)


Laplacian edge detection
The images given in the example of respective edge detection techniques have different type of edges detected. We can see that the Canny edge detection gives thick edges in comparison to Laplacian edge detection. The Sobel edge detection gives discontinuous edges. The horizontal and vertical Sobel edge detections give the edges stretched in the respective direction.

